2026-03-20 13:46:23,768 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 1336, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 519, "content": "You are product_manager_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Your role is abstract workflow planning only. Design how the workflow should behave stage by stage, but do not select node types, do not mention n8n nodes, do not mention credentials, do not mention parameter names, do not mention API endpoints, and do not generate workflow JSON. You are preparing a clean handoff for a future architect_agent that will later ground the plan into nodes. Preserve the user's exact semantics instead of broadening the request.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 3442, "content": "Create an abstract workflow plan from this request context.\n\nOriginal workflow request: crea un workflow para coger los emails que vaya recibiendo y que los clasifique por nivel de urgencia con IA\nUse case title: crea un workflow para coger los emails que vaya recibiendo y que los clasifiq...\nBusiness problem: User requested a new workflow for: crea un workflow para coger los emails que vaya recibiendo y que los clasifique por nivel de urgencia con IA\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: crea un workflow para coger los emails que vaya recibiendo y que los clasifique por nivel de urgencia con IA\nExpected business value: Provide a high-quality workflow plan ready for architectural grounding.\nClarifications already provided:\n-\n\nRules:\n- Output planning-level stages only.\n- If the request contains more than one explicit workflow operation, return at least 2 stages.\n- Otherwise return the minimum number of stages that still covers the full request coherently.\n- Each stage must define purpose, required_capabilities, expected_inputs, expected_outputs, dependencies, and success_criteria.\n- Each stage must have one dominant operable action that the workflow can actually execute.\n- Stages must describe behavior, not implementation details.\n- Do not mix source intake with downstream classification, storage, notification, or source mutation in the same stage.\n- User-visible outcomes like filtering, visibility, browsing, or 'seeing items in Gmail' belong in user_visible_goal or success_criteria, not as the primary action of a stage.\n- Preserve the exact source system, trigger style, processing mode, and final outcome named by the user.\n- Determine whether the workflow ends in a useful business effect, such as applying, saving, notifying, routing to a concrete downstream action, or intentionally exposing the result to the user.\n- If the workflow would otherwise end only in a classification, decision, routing outcome, or transformation result, ask what should happen with that result unless the user explicitly wants analysis or reporting only.\n- If the user said heuristic, rule-based, deterministic, manual, inbound, outgoing, receive, or send, keep that distinction explicit in the plan.\n- Distinguish receiving email from sending email; they are not interchangeable.\n- explicit_user_operations must list the canonical workflow operations explicitly requested by the user.\n- covered_operations must list the canonical workflow operations materially covered by the returned stages.\n- Do not leave requested operations covered only in workflow_summary, assumptions, data_flow, or handoff_notes; they must appear in real stages.\n- Do not invent validation, feedback, manual review, refinement, or approval stages unless the user explicitly asked for them.\n- Never output concrete node types or workflow JSON.\n- If the user explicitly named systems like Gmail, Slack, or Google Sheets, treat them as business/system context, not node choices.\n- Set planning_ready=true only if the abstract workflow plan is coherent enough to hand off to architect_agent.\n- If essential planning information is missing, set planning_ready=false and list the missing_information as concise user-facing clarification questions.\n- Write missing_information questions in the same language as the user's request.\n- handoff_notes must explain what architect_agent should preserve when grounding this plan into nodes.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "local-model", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.2}, "request_id": "75e44a038e", "stage": "multi_agent.product_manager.abstract_plan", "total_chars": 3961, "ts_utc": "2026-03-20T12:46:23.768434+00:00"}
2026-03-20 13:46:36,865 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 3901, "content_preview": "{\"workflow_summary\":\"This workflow captures incoming emails and classifies them by urgency level using AI, without specifying further downstream actions.\",\"stages\":[{\"id\":\"stage_1\",\"name\":\"Capture Incoming Emails\",\"purpose\":\"Continuously receive and store incoming emails as they arrive.\",\"stage_kind\":\"trigger_intake\",\"business_effect\":\"The user will see new emails appear in their email system, but no further action is taken on them yet.\",\"target_entity\":\"email\",\"user_visible_goal\":\"The user can browse and see incoming emails as they arrive.\",\"unresolved_decisions\":[\"What email system (e.g., Gmail) should be used to receive the emails?\",\"Should the workflow only process new emails or also existing ones?\"],\"required_capabilities\":[\"Receive emails in real-time or near-real-time\",\"Store received emails persistently\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"Incoming email messages (subject, body, sender, timestamp, etc.)\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"A collection of stored emails ready for classification\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"success_criteria\":[\"All incoming emails are captured and stored without loss or duplication\",\"The user can see new emails in their email system as they arrive\"],\"notes\":\"This stage focuses solely on intake; no processing, classification, or downstream action is attempted here.\"},{\"id\":\"stage_2\",\"name\":\"Classify Emails by Urgency with AI\",\"purpose\":\"Analyze each stored email and assign it an urgency level using AI.\",\"stage_kind\":\"classify_decision\",\"business_effect\":\"Emails are now tagged with an urgency label, but this result is not yet used or exposed to the user.\",\"target_entity\":\"email\",\"user_visible_goal\":\"The user will eventually see emails labeled by urgency, but visibility is not part of this stage.\",\"unresolved_decisions\":[\"What AI model or service should perform the urgency classification?\",\"How many urgency levels (e.g., low, medium, high) are needed?\"],\"required_capabilities\":[\"Apply an AI model to analyze email content and metadata\",\"Output a discrete urgency label for each email\"],\"expected_inputs\":[\"A collection of stored emails from the previous stage\"],\"expected_outputs\":[\"Emails annotated with an urgency level (e.g., low, medium, high)\"],\"dependencies\":[\"Stage 1: Capture Incoming Emails must complete successfully to provide input emails.\"],\"success_criteria\":[\"Every email receives a single, consistent urgency label\",\"The AI classification is accurate and reflects the user’s expectations of urgency\"],\"notes\":\"This stage performs pure classification; no storage, notification, or routing occurs here. The architect must decide what to do with the classified emails (e.g., store, notify, route).\"}],\"data_flow\":[{\"source_stage_id\":\"stage_1\",\"target_stage_id\":\"stage_2\",\"data_items\":[\"Stored email messages\"],\"notes\":\"Data flows from intake to classification without transformation or enrichment.\"}],\"assumptions\":[\"The user only wants to classify emails by urgency and does not need further downstream actions (e.g., routing, notifications).\",\"The AI model for urgency classification is already available or will be provided later.\"],\"missing_information\":[\"What should happen with the classified emails? Should they be stored, notified, routed to a specific folder, or exposed to the user in some way?\",\"Which email system (e.g., Gmail) should be used for intake and visibility?\"],\"handoff_notes\":[\"Preserve the exact trigger style: receive incoming emails without filtering.\",\"Preserve the exact processing mode: classify each email independently with AI.\",\"Do not implement storage, notification, or routing in this plan; those are downstream decisions.\",\"The architect must decide how to handle the classified output (e.g., store, notify, route).\"],\"explicit_user_operations